{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.InterfaceOperatorBlockDiagonal","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.InterfaceOperatorBlockDiagonal","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Ring.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.InterfaceOperator.trace_eq_sum_interfaceBlock","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.InterfaceOperator.trace_eq_sum_interfaceBlock","kind":"theorem","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/InterfaceOperatorBlockDiagonal.lean#L142-L155","doc":"Restatement of `trace_block_diagonal` in terms of the named\n`interfaceBlock` compressions `A_i = P i · I · P i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.InterfaceOperator.trace_block_diagonal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.InterfaceOperator.trace_block_diagonal","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/InterfaceOperatorBlockDiagonal.lean#L84-L140","doc":"**Block-diagonality of the interface operator under a cyclic trace.**\n\nLet `{P i}` be an orthogonal resolution of unity in `A` (`P i · P j = 0` for\n`i ≠ j`, and `Σ i, P i = 1`). Let `W, β ∈ A` each commute with every `P i`, and\nlet `τ : A →+ R` be cyclic (`τ (x*y) = τ (y*x)`). Then the trace of `W · I · β`\ncollapses onto the diagonal compressions of `I`:\n\n  `τ (W · I · β) = Σ i, τ ( W · (P i · I · P i) · β )`.\n\nThis is the \"only the diagonal isotypic block survives the closed trace\"\ninvariant from the closure-(b) design — the structural reason the interface\noperator `A^λ_{ξν}(I) = P_{ξν} ρ_λ(I) P_{ξν}` is universal by construction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.InterfaceOperator.interfaceBlock","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.InterfaceOperator.interfaceBlock","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/InterfaceOperatorBlockDiagonal.lean#L79-L82","doc":"The diagonal isotypic block of the interface operator:\n`A_i = P i · I · P i`, the compression of `I = ρ_λ(I)` to the\n`i = (ξ,ν)` isotypic sector. ","signatureChunk":0}]}